content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 2.0 mm/s is in Zone A (0.0-2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines') on the HF-300 severity chart (Figure 3), well below the 4.5 mm/s 'plan maintenance' boundary and the 7.1 mm/s 'stop the pump' boundary. No vibration action is required. This assumes the reading is RMS velocity and is the highest of the two bearing housings, as the manual requires.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 65 C is within the manual limit (normal up to 70 C; alarm 80 C; trip 90 C). Bearing temperature is measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Flow has dropped about 20% at unchanged valve settings, against a rated duty of 300 m3/h at 45 m. This matches the 'Low flow or head' symptom in the troubleshooting table. The current absolute flow and head were not reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported at the shaft seal, so seal replacement is not indicated by the symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn impeller and/or wear rings. This is consistent with a gradual loss of flow at the same valve settings while vibration and bearing temperature stay normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Air in the suction or casing. The corrective action is to vent the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A closed or partly closed valve (for example a suction-side valve or a blockage). This is less likely because valve settings are reported unchanged, but it should still be verified.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. With the pump running, record suction and discharge conditions and confirm actual valve positions on both suction and discharge lines. Re-measure vibration on BOTH bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Vent the casing to remove any trapped air and check the suction for air ingress. Do not allow the seal to run dry: it is flushed by Plan 11 from the pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. If flow does not recover, isolate and drain the pump, then remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment (68 kg). The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller and wear rings for wear or damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. If the seal or sleeve is disturbed, inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Do not refit or fit seal HF3-450 on this serial; fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, which is pre-set and needs no sleeve measurement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Reassemble with a new casing gasket. Tighten fasteners as follows (lightly oiled threads): impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm (if disturbed). Tighten seal gland nuts on HF3-450B to 30 Nm, not the 25 Nm in Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. If the motor or bearing housing was moved, laser-align the shaft to within 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Return to service. Confirm the seal flush is established before running, then verify flow at the same valve settings. Record vibration (Zone A target) and housing temperature (normal up to 70 C).",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above). Contingency only: required if the seal is disturbed or found damaged.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency only: replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate (lock out) and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg; use lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The seal is flushed by Plan 11 from the pump discharge, so ensure the casing is vented and primed before starting.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump if vibration reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS). Respond to a bearing housing alarm at 80 C; the trip is at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "There is no standard time for impeller and wear ring inspection. As a reference, back pull-out work for a mechanical seal replacement is 4.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, if the motor or bearing housing is moved: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal part: the manual's procedure and Table 5 assume the original seal (HF3-450). Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. P-112 is serial HF3-22300, so the bulletin applies: use HF3-450B, never HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Serial HF3-22300 is within the bulletin range, so 30 Nm applies. All other Table 5 torques remain valid.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling: manual 5.2 step 4 requires inspecting the sleeve for scoring. SB-2026-014 says no sleeve measurement is needed for setting the pre-set HF3-450B, but still requires replacing sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. Apply the bulletin: visually inspect for scoring depth only.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Wear ring clearance limits and impeller wear acceptance criteria are not given in the evidence.",
    "Part numbers for the impeller, wear rings and casing gasket are not available; the parts list (section 2 / Figure 2) has no part names or numbers.",
    "Current absolute flow, suction pressure and NPSH available were not reported, so suction-side problems cannot be confirmed or excluded.",
    "It is not confirmed that the 2.0 mm/s reading is RMS velocity and the highest of both bearing housings.",
    "Coupling type is unknown, so it is unclear whether the motor must be moved during back pull-out (which would trigger laser alignment).",
    "There is no standard labour time for impeller and wear ring inspection or replacement.",
    "The process criticality and production impact of the 20% flow loss are unknown; priority may need adjusting."
  ]
}
